  <編章節>      Section 4 Virtual Asset Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 12</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The criteria for identifying abnormal virtual asset accounts or transactions suspected of involvement in fraud are as follows:
1. The applicant frequently applies for virtual asset accounts over a short period of time without reasonable explanation.
2. The transaction functions requested by the customer are obviously inconsistent with the customer's age or background.
3. The contact information provided by the customer cannot be verified by using reasonable measures.
4. The virtual asset account has been reported by a virtual asset service provider, financial institution, government agency, or a member of the general public as being used by someone suspected of criminal activity.
5. The virtual asset account has been used with frequent small-amount inward and outward remittances suspected of being probing activities.
6. The customer makes frequent use of the services or facilities of virtual asset service providers within a short period of time in a manner that is obviously at variance with the normal transaction activities of the customer.
7. An inactive virtual asset account with unexpected unusual transactions.
8. A virtual asset account whose holder provides the same mobile phone number as that provided by the customer of another watch-listed virtual asset account in the same virtual asset service provider, and which is suspected to be used for criminal activity.
9. A non-Taiwanese person who is found by a virtual asset service provider to have had relevant identity certification documents, such as resident certificates provided for verification upon the opening of a virtual asset account, revoked prior to expiration, to have overstayed, or to have been reported as missing.
10. A customer who is verified by a virtual asset service provider to have been reported as a missing person.
11. A domestic virtual asset account listed by a judicial police authority as suspected of involvement in fraud.
12. A virtual asset account with transactions that show signs of involvement in fraud, as set out in the Anti-Money Laundering, Counter-Terrorism Financing, and Anti-Fraud Crime and Industry Joint Defense Mechanisms and other self-regulatory rules of the Taiwan Virtual Asset Service Provider Association.
13. Other abnormal virtual asset accounts or transactions determined by the competent authority or virtual asset service providers to be suspected of involvement in fraud.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
