  <編章節>   Chapter 3 Recordkeeping and Notification of Data Transactions and Account Management</編章節>
  <編章節>      Section 1 Deposit Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 15</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When deposit business institutions implement measures in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act, they shall retain the following information and transaction records in hard copy or electronic format:
1. All records obtained through CDD measures, such as copies or records of passports, identity cards, driving licenses or other similar official identification documents of the account holder.
2. Contract files.
3. All abnormal transaction records of deposit accounts suspected of involvement in fraud.
4. Data and records obtained from inquiries regarding abnormal deposit accounts suspected of involvement in fraud in accordance with regulations in Chapter 2.
The abnormal transaction records of deposit accounts suspected of involvement in fraud, as referred to in Subparagraph 3 of the preceding paragraph, shall be sufficient to reconstruct individual abnormal transactions and serve as evidence for identifying illegal activity.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 16</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Where a deposit account is identified as an abnormal deposit account suspected of involvement in fraud, the deposit business institution shall take the following response measures:
1. It shall strengthen the CDD measures for the account holder in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act. It may adopt control measures such as continual review, suspension of deposits or withdrawals, suspension of outward remittance of funds, suspension of all or certain transaction functions, and refusal to establish a business relationship or to provide services, and may report to the judicial police authority.
2. If a virtual account is watch-listed, the deposit business institution shall suspend all transaction functions of the virtual account and earmark an amount in the deposit account that corresponds to the amount in the virtual account. Subsequent inward remittances of the virtual account shall be returned to the deposit business institution or electronic payment institution that conducted the remittance by refund. If there is no outward remittance account corresponding to the virtual account to which the remittance can be returned, the deposit business institution shall earmark the amount in the virtual account. The deposit business institution shall immediately notify the account holder to take relevant control measures with regard to the user of the virtual account.
3. If the watch-listed virtual account is a virtual account under a trust deposit account of a virtual asset service provider that is held in custody by a deposit business institution, the deposit business institution shall immediately notify the virtual asset service provider. After receiving the notification from the deposit business institution, the virtual asset service provider shall check whether all or part of the reported fraud-related funds remain in the virtual account, and provide the results to the receiving deposit business institution.
4. Measures to be taken in accordance with the Money Laundering Control Act and other applicable laws and regulations.
When a deposit business institution notifies the judicial police in accordance with the regulations in the preceding paragraph, it shall use the telephone, fax, email, electronic platform, or other feasible means. It shall also provide documents of abnormal deposit accounts suspected of involvement in fraud, the identity of the account holder, relevant transaction records, or other documents required to be provided under the notification method based on the request.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 17</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After receiving a report from the deposit business institution, the judicial police authority shall notify the deposit business institution by official letter within 20 days whether to continue or lift the control measures imposed on the abnormal deposit account suspected of involvement in fraud. If the judicial police authority fails to notify the deposit business institution within this period, the deposit business institution may continue to apply the control measures.
In case of major contingencies, the judicial police authority may send the notification in the preceding paragraph to the deposit business institution by telephone, fax, email, or other feasible means, followed by a confirming official letter and documents which should be delivered within five business days.
If an account holder has any doubts regarding the control measures implemented by the deposit business institution with respect to his or her deposit account in accordance with the notification from the judicial police authority, he or she may contact the deposit business institution for inquiries, and may also contact the original judicial police authority that notified the implementation of the control measures where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 2 Electronic Payment Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 18</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When electronic payment institutions implement measures in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act, they shall retain the following information and transaction records in hard copy or electronic format:
1. All records obtained through CDD measures, such as copies or records of passports, identity cards, or other similar official identification documents of the user.
2. Contract files.
3. All abnormal transaction records of electronic payment accounts suspected of involvement in fraud.
4. Data and records obtained from inquiries regarding abnormal electronic payment accounts suspected of involvement in fraud in accordance with regulations in Chapter 2.
The abnormal transaction records of electronic payment accounts suspected of involvement in fraud, as referred to in Subparagraph 3 of the preceding paragraph, shall be sufficient to reconstruct individual abnormal transactions, and shall serve as evidence for identifying illegal activity.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 19</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Where an electronic payment account is identified as an abnormal electronic payment account suspected of involvement in fraud, the electronic payment institution shall take the following measures:
1. It shall strengthen the CDD measures for the user in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act. It may adopt control measures such as continual review, suspension of inward remittances (transfers) or withdrawals, suspension of all or part of the transaction functions, refusal to establish a business relationship or to provide services, and may report to the judicial police authority.
2. Measures to be taken in accordance with the Money Laundering Control Act and other applicable laws and regulations.
When the electronic payment institution reports to the judicial police authority in accordance with the regulations in the preceding paragraph, it shall use the telephone, fax, email, electronic platform, or other feasible means. The institution shall also provide relevant documents related to the suspicious electronic payment accounts, the user’s identity information, relevant transaction records, or other documents required to be provided under the reporting.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 20</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After receiving a report from the electronic payment institution, the judicial police authority shall notify the electronic payment institution by official letter within 20 days whether to continue or lift the control measures imposed on the abnormal electronic payment account suspected of involvement in fraud. If the judicial police authority fails to notify the electronic payment institution within this period, the electronic payment institution may continue to apply the control measures.
In case of major contingencies, the judicial police authority may send the notification in the preceding paragraph to the electronic payment institution by telephone, fax, email, or other feasible means, followed by a confirming official letter and documents which should be delivered within five business days.
If a user has any doubts regarding the control measures implemented by the electronic payment institution with respect to his or her electronic payment account in accordance with the notification from the judicial police authority, he or she may contact the electronic payment institution for inquiries, and may also contact the original judicial police authority that notified the implementation of the control measures where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 3 Credit Cards</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 21</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When card issuers implement measures in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act, they shall retain the following information and transaction records in hard copy or electronic format:
1. All records obtained through CDD measures, such as copies or records of passports, identity cards, driving licenses or other similar official identification documents of the cardholder.
2. Contract files.
3. All abnormal transaction records of credit cards suspected of involvement in fraud.
4. Data and records obtained from inquiries regarding abnormal credit cards suspected of involvement in fraud in accordance with regulations in Chapter 2.
The abnormal transaction records of credit cards suspected of involvement in fraud, as referred to in Subparagraph 3 of the preceding paragraph, shall be sufficient to reconstruct individual abnormal transactions and shall serve as evidence for identifying illegal activity.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 22</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Where a credit card is identified as an abnormal credit card suspected of involvement in fraud, the card issuer shall take the following response measures:
1. It shall strengthen the CDD measures for the customer in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act. It may adopt control measures such as continual review, credit card management, suspension of credit card account transaction functions, and refusal to establish a business relationship or to provide services, and may report to the judicial police authority.
2. Measures to be taken in accordance with the Money Laundering Control Act and other applicable laws and regulations.
When a card issuer notifies the judicial police authority in accordance with the regulations in the preceding paragraph, it shall use the telephone, fax, email, electronic platform, or other feasible means. It shall also provide documents of abnormal credit cards suspected of involvement in fraud, the identity of the cardholder, relevant transaction records, or other documents required to be provided under the notification method based on the request.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 23</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After receiving a report from the card issuer, the judicial police authority shall notify the card issuer by official letter within 20 days whether to continue or lift the control measures imposed on the abnormal credit card suspected of involvement in fraud. If the judicial police authority fails to notify the card issuer within this period, the card issuer may continue to apply the control measures.
In case of major contingencies, the judicial police authority may send the notification in the preceding paragraph to the card issuer by telephone, fax, email, or other feasible means, followed by a confirming official letter and documents which should be delivered within five business days.
If a cardholder has any doubts regarding the control measures implemented by the card issuer with respect to his or her credit card in accordance with the notification from the judicial police authority, he or she may contact the card issuer for inquiries, and may also contact the original judicial police authority that notified the implementation of the control measures where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 4 Virtual Asset Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 24</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When virtual asset service providers implement measures in accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act, they shall retain the following information and transaction records in hard copy or electronic format:
1. All records obtained through CDD measures, such as copies or records of passports, identity cards, driving licenses or other similar official identification documents of the customer.
2. Contract files.
3. All abnormal transaction records of virtual asset accounts suspected of involvement in fraud.
4. Data and records obtained from inquiries regarding abnormal virtual asset accounts suspected of involvement in fraud in accordance with regulations in Chapter 2.
The abnormal transaction records of virtual asset accounts suspected of involvement in fraud, as referred to in Subparagraph 3 of the preceding paragraph, shall be sufficient to reconstruct individual abnormal transactions and shall serve as evidence for identifying illegal activity.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 25</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a virtual asset account is identified as an abnormal virtual asset account suspected of involvement in fraud, the virtual asset service provider shall take the following measures:
1. In accordance with the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act, the virtual asset service provider shall strengthen the CDD measures for the customer and may adopt control measures such as continual review, suspension of deposits or withdrawals, suspension of outward remittance of virtual assets and funds, suspension of all or partial transaction functions, and refusal to establish a business relationship, service provision, and other control measures, and may report to the judicial police authority.
2. Measures to be taken in accordance with the Money Laundering Control Act and other applicable laws and regulations.
When a virtual asset service provider notifies the judicial police authority in accordance with the regulations in the preceding paragraph, it shall use the telephone, fax, email, electronic platform, or other feasible means. The virtual asset service provider shall also provide documents of abnormal virtual asset accounts suspected of involvement in fraud, the identity of the customer, relevant transaction records, or other documents required to be provided under the notification method.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 26</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After receiving a report from the virtual asset service provider, the judicial police authority shall notify the virtual asset service provider by official letter within 20 days whether to continue or lift the control measures imposed on the abnormal virtual asset account suspected of involvement in fraud. If the judicial police authority fails to notify the virtual asset service provider within this period, the virtual asset service provider may continue to apply the control measures.
In case of major contingencies, the judicial police authority may send the notification in the preceding paragraph to the virtual asset service provider by telephone, fax, email, or other feasible means, followed by a confirming official letter and documents which should be delivered within five business days after the initial notification.
If a customer has any doubts regarding the control measures implemented by the virtual asset service provider with respect to his or her virtual asset account in accordance with the notification from the judicial police authority, he or she may contact the virtual asset service provider for inquiries, and may also contact the original judicial police authority that notified the implementation of the control measures where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>   Chapter 4 Joint Defense Reporting System and Earmarking of Funds</編章節>
  <編章節>      Section 1 Deposit Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 27</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[For a deposit account reported as a watch-listed account, the deposit business institution shall verify the source of the notification, classify it as a watch-listed account, and check related transactions of the account. If the deposit business institution finds that funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted to another deposit account, an electronic payment account, or a virtual asset account, the deposit business institution shall notify the receiving deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider of the remittance of such amount.
The receiving deposit business institution shall immediately review the transactions of the recipient account after receiving a notification made by the previous receiving institution or the virtual asset service provider. If the funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted to another account, the deposit business institution shall notify the next receiving deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider of the outward transfer information.
If the deposit business institution holding the trust deposit account linked to the virtual asset account finds that the funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted into a virtual account under such trust deposit account, it shall immediately notify the virtual asset service provider to investigate whether all or part of the funds reported as fraudulent remain in the virtual account. The virtual asset service provider shall report the inquiry results to the deposit business institution holding the trust deposit account. The deposit business institution shall report the inquiry results to the original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed account.
If the recipient deposit business institution discovers that the funds reported as fraudulent have been withdrawn, it shall notify the original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed deposit account.
The original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed deposit account shall verify the information listed in the preceding paragraph. If the original judicial police authority determines that the receiving account or virtual asset account shall also be classified as a watch-listed account, it shall notify the relevant deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider to classify such account or account number as a watch-listed account.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 28</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a victim of fraud visits a deposit business institution during its business hours to report that he or she has been defrauded, the deposit business institution shall confirm his or her identity, remittance or transfer information, and the reason for the fraud. The victim shall then be asked to fill out an affidavit and call the 165 hotline.
The deposit business institution shall notify the recipient deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider based on the affidavit and remittance or transfer information in the preceding paragraph. The inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article shall apply mutatis mutandis if the recipient deposit business institution receives a notification from the previous deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider.
If a fraud victim visits a deposit business institution in person to inform the institution of the fraud, in accordance with Paragraph 1, the police authority shall send an officer to the deposit business institution within two hours to process the victim’s report and, if necessary, classify the deposit account as watch-listed.
After receiving the notification from the police authority in the preceding paragraph, the deposit business institution shall process the notification in accordance with the inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 29</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The contents of the joint defense notifications in the preceding two articles shall be registered in the manner prescribed by the authority responsible for sending the watch-listed deposit account notification.
The contents of the joint defense notification, format of the notification form and the affidavit, and other detailed items for the notifications shall be formulated by the Bankers Association of the Republic of China and reported to the competent authority for record.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 30</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After a deposit business institution receives a notification from the previous deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider, it shall earmark the amount received based on the notification. If the account balance is less than the notified amount, the current balance in the account shall be earmarked. The amount of funds or virtual assets earmarked by each deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, and virtual asset service provider for the same notification shall be capped at the amount of the fraudulent funds specified in the notification from the judicial police authority that provided the original notification or the amount of the fraudulent funds or virtual assets specified by the victim in his or her affidavit.
The recipient deposit business institution shall notify the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed deposit account of the results of the earmarking.
After receiving the notification in the preceding paragraph, the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed deposit account shall verify the results as soon as possible and notify the deposit business institution within 48 hours from the time of the earmarking regarding whether the deposit account with the earmarked amount should be classified as watch-listed or whether the earmarking should be released.
If the deposit business institution does not receive a notification within the period specified in the preceding paragraph regarding the deposit account with the earmarked amount to be classified as watch-listed, it shall release the earmarking.
The deposit business institution may release the earmarked funds in advance if it determines, after careful verification, that there is no illegal or abnormal circumstance in the deposit account specified in the earmarking notification.
The deposit business institution shall continuously monitor the deposit accounts with earmarked amounts, and if it determines that the account is an abnormal deposit account suspected of involvement in fraud, it may process the account in accordance with Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 31</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the funds in a deposit account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the deposit business institution subsequently receives a notification for the earmarking of proceeds of fraud in the deposit account, the deposit business institution shall still be required to earmark the proceeds of fraud, but priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure for such funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 32</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Deposit business institutions shall, to the extent possible, set up a dedicated 24-hour joint defense notification contact window to carry out the joint defense notification mechanisms.
Deposit business institutions shall immediately notify Financial Information Service Co., Ltd. when they set up the contact window in the preceding paragraph, and the same applies when the contact window is changed.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 33</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the account holder of a deposit account with seized funds has any doubts regarding the seizure of his/her funds, he or she should contact the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed deposit account to resolve the matter. The deposit business institution shall also provide assistance where necessary.
If a deposit business institution conducts joint defense operations but no facts of fraud are found in subsequent investigations and the customer's rights and interests are damaged due to the deposit business institution's joint defense notification or the earmarking of funds results in a dishonored check, the deposit business institution shall assist in applying to the Taiwan Clearing House for the cancellation of dishonored check records or take other remedial measures.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 2 Electronic Payment Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 34</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When an electronic payment account is reported as a watch-listed account, the electronic payment institution, in addition to verifying the source of the notification, shall classify it as a watch-listed account, and immediately review the related transactions of the account. If the electronic payment institution finds that funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted to another deposit account, electronic payment account, or virtual asset account, the electronic payment institution shall notify the receiving deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider of the remitted amount.
The receiving electronic payment institution shall immediately review the transactions of the recipient account after receiving a notification made by the previous receiving institution or the virtual asset service provider. If the funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted to another account, the electronic payment institution shall notify the next receiving deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider of the outward transfer information. If the funds are not remitted, it shall notify the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed electronic payment account.
The original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed electronic payment account shall verify the information listed in the preceding paragraph. If the original judicial police authority determines that the receiving account or virtual asset account shall also be classified as a watch-listed account, it shall notify the relevant electronic payment institution, deposit business institution, or virtual asset service provider to classify such account or account number as a watch-listed account.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 35</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a victim of fraud visits an electronic payment institution to report that he or she has been defrauded, the electronic payment institution shall confirm his or her identity, certification of electronic payment account transactions, and the reason for the fraud. The victim shall then be asked to fill out an affidavit and call the 165 hotline. When a victim of fraud calls the customer service of an electronic payment institution to report a fraud, the electronic payment institution shall refer the victim to the 165 hotline.
The electronic payment institution shall notify the receiving deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider based on the affidavit and the electronic payment account transaction certification in the preceding paragraph. The inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article shall apply mutatis mutandis if the receiving electronic payment institution receives a notification from the previous deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider.
If a fraud victim visits an electronic payment institution in person to inform the institution of the fraud, the police authority shall send an officer to the electronic payment institution within two hours to process the victim’s report and, if necessary, classify the electronic payment account as watch-listed.
After receiving the notification from the police authority in the preceding paragraph, the electronic payment institution shall process the notification in accordance with the inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 36</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The contents of the joint defense notifications in the preceding two articles shall be registered in the manner prescribed by the authority responsible for sending the watch-listed electronic payment account notification.
The contents of the joint defense notification, format of the notification form and the affidavit, and other detailed items for the notifications shall be formulated by the Electronic Payment Association of R.O.C. and reported to the competent authority for record.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 37</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After an electronic payment institution receives a notification from the previous deposit business institution, electronic payment institution, or virtual asset service provider, it shall earmark the amount received based on the notification. If the account balance is less than the notified amount, the current balance in the account shall be earmarked. The amount of funds or virtual assets earmarked by each electronic payment institution, deposit business institution, and virtual asset service provider for the same notification shall be capped at the amount of the fraudulent funds specified in the notification from the judicial police authority that provided the original notification or the amount of the fraudulent funds or virtual assets specified by the victim in his or her affidavit.
The electronic payment institution shall notify the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed electronic payment account of the results of the earmarking.
After receiving the notification in the preceding paragraph, the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed electronic payment account shall verify the results as soon as possible and notify the electronic payment institution within 48 hours from the time of the earmarking regarding whether the electronic payment account with the earmarked amount should be classified as watch-listed or whether the earmarking should be released.
If the electronic payment institution does not receive a notification for classifying the electronic payment account as watch-listed within the period specified in the preceding paragraph, the electronic payment institution shall release the earmarking.
The electronic payment institution may release the earmarked funds in advance if it determines, after careful verification, that there is no illegal or abnormal circumstance in the electronic payment account specified in the earmarking notification.
The electronic payment institution shall continuously monitor the electronic payment accounts with earmarked amounts, and if it determines that the account is an abnormal electronic payment account suspected of involvement in fraud, it may process the account in accordance with Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 38</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the funds in an electronic payment account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the electronic payment institution subsequently receives a notification for the earmarking of proceeds of fraud in the electronic payment account, the electronic payment institution shall still be required to earmark the proceeds of fraud, but priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure for such funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 39</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Electronic payment institutions shall, to the extent possible, set up a dedicated 24-hour joint defense notification contact window to carry out the joint defense notification mechanisms.
Electronic payment institutions shall immediately notify Financial Information Service Co., Ltd. when they set up the contact window in the preceding paragraph, and the same applies when the contact window is changed.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 40</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the user of an electronic payment account with seized funds has any doubts regarding the seizure of his or her funds, he or she shall contact the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed account to resolve the matter. The electronic payment institution shall also provide assistance where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 3 Credit Cards</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 41</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Where a credit card settlement number is reported as a watch-listed credit card settlement number, the card issuer shall immediately suspend all transaction functions of the credit card and disable the payment functions for automatic payment channels. This restriction does not apply if the card issuer verifies that payment is made by the cardholder.
If the card issuer finds that funds reported as fraudulent have been remitted to another deposit account or an electronic payment account held by the cardholder, the card issuer shall notify the next receiving deposit business institution or electronic payment institution as well as the judicial police authority that reported the credit card settlement number as watch-listed.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 42</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a victim of fraud calls the customer service of a card issuer to report a fraud, the card issuer shall refer the victim to the 165 hotline.
When a victim of fraud visits a card issuer during its business hours to report that he or she has been defrauded, the card issuer shall confirm his or her identity, remittance or transfer information, and the reason for the fraud, and call the 165 hotline. The police authority shall send an officer to the card issuer within two hours to accept the case report from the victim and, if necessary, classify the credit card settlement number as watch-listed.
After receiving the notification from the police authority in the preceding paragraph, the card issuer shall process the notification in accordance with the inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 43</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The contents of the joint defense notifications in the preceding two articles shall be registered in the manner prescribed by the authority responsible for sending the watch-listed credit card settlement number notification.
The contents and format of the joint defense notification and other detailed items for the notifications shall be formulated by the Bankers Association of the Republic of China and reported to the competent authority for record.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 44</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The card issuers shall, to the extent possible, set up a dedicated 24-hour joint defense notification contact window to carry out the joint defense notification mechanisms.
The card issuers shall immediately notify Financial Information Service Co., Ltd. when they set up the contact window in the preceding paragraph, and the same applies when the contact window is changed.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 4 Virtual Asset Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 45</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[For a virtual asset account reported as a watch-listed virtual asset account, the virtual asset service provider, in addition to verifying the source of the report and classifying it as a watch-listed virtual asset account, shall suspend all transaction functions of the account and investigate related transactions. If the virtual asset service provider finds that the reported fraud-related virtual assets have been remitted to another virtual asset service provider or remitted in the form of fiat currency to another deposit account, virtual account, or electronic payment account, it shall notify the receiving virtual asset service provider, the receiving deposit business institution, or the electronic payment institution of the outward transfer information of the virtual assets.
The receiving virtual asset service provider shall immediately investigate the transactions of the recipient account after receiving the notification made by the previous virtual asset service provider or receiving institution. If the virtual assets have been remitted or remitted in the form of fiat currency to another deposit account, virtual account, or electronic payment account, it shall notify the next receiving virtual asset service provider, or the next receiving deposit business institution or electronic payment institution, of the outward transfer information of the virtual assets.
If the receiving virtual asset service provider finds that fraudulent virtual assets reported have been withdrawn or remitted to an offshore virtual asset account, it shall notify the original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed virtual asset account.
The original judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed virtual asset account shall verify the information listed in the preceding paragraph. If the original judicial police authority determines that the receiving virtual asset account or recipient account into which such virtual assets were transferred shall also be classified as watch-listed, it shall notify the relevant virtual asset service provider, deposit business institution, or electronic payment institution to classify such account as watch-listed.
For the purpose of fraud crime prevention, virtual asset service providers may notify the deposit business institution holding the trust deposit account linked to a watch-listed virtual asset account, or the deposit business institution or electronic payment institution holding the bound deposit account or electronic payment account, of information related to the watch-listed virtual asset account or fraudulent virtual assets. Deposit business institutions or electronic payment institutions may, based on the relevant information provided by virtual asset service providers, implement control measures provided in the latter part of Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 46</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a victim of fraud visits a virtual asset service provider during its business hours to report that he or she has been defrauded, the virtual asset service provider shall confirm his or her identity, the transfer of virtual assets or funds, remittance or transfer information, and the reason for the fraud. The victim shall then be asked to fill out an affidavit and call the 165 hotline. When a victim of fraud calls the customer service of a virtual asset service provider to report a fraud, the virtual asset service provider shall refer the victim to the 165 hotline.
The virtual asset service provider shall notify the receiving virtual asset service provider, receiving deposit business institution, or electronic payment institution based on the affidavit and remittance or transfer information in the preceding paragraph. The inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article shall apply mutatis mutandis if the virtual asset service provider of the recipient account receives a notification from the previous virtual asset service provider, deposit business institution, or electronic payment institution.
If a fraud victim visits a virtual asset service provider in person to inform the service provider of the fraud, in accordance with Paragraph 1, the police authority shall send an officer to the virtual asset service provider within two hours to process the victim’s report and, if necessary, classify the virtual asset account as watch-listed.
After receiving the notification from the police authority in the preceding paragraph, the virtual asset service provider shall process the notification in accordance with the inquiry and notification procedures in the preceding article.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 47</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[The contents of the joint defense notifications in the preceding two articles shall be registered in the manner prescribed by the authority responsible for sending the watch-listed virtual asset account notification.
The contents of the joint defense notification, format of the notification form and the affidavit, and other detailed items for the notifications shall be formulated by the Taiwan Virtual Asset Service Provider Association and reported to the competent authority for record.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 48</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[After a virtual asset service provider receives a notification from the previous virtual asset service provider, deposit business institution, or electronic payment institution, it shall earmark an amount based on the virtual assets or funds specified in the notification. If the account balance is less than the notified amount, the current balance of virtual assets or funds in the account shall be earmarked. The amount of virtual assets or funds earmarked by each virtual asset service provider, deposit business institution, and electronic payment institution for the same notification shall be capped at the amount of the fraudulent funds specified in the notification from the judicial police authority that provided the original notification for the virtual asset account or the amount of the fraudulent virtual assets or funds specified by the victim in his or her affidavit.
The virtual asset service provider shall notify the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed virtual asset account of the results of the earmarking.
After receiving the notification in the preceding paragraph, the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed virtual asset account shall verify the results as soon as possible and notify the virtual asset service provider within 48 hours from the time of the earmarking regarding whether the virtual asset account with the earmarked amount should be classified as watch-listed or whether the earmarking should be released.
If the virtual asset service provider does not receive a notification for classifying the virtual asset account with the earmarked virtual assets or funds as watch-listed within the period specified in the preceding paragraph, the virtual asset service provider shall release the earmarking.
The virtual asset service provider may release the earmarked virtual assets or funds in advance if it determines, after careful verification, that there is no illegal or abnormal circumstance in the virtual asset account specified in the earmarking notification.
The virtual asset service provider shall continuously monitor the virtual asset accounts with earmarked virtual assets or funds, and if it determines that the account is an abnormal virtual asset account suspected of involvement in fraud, it may process the account in accordance with Paragraph 1, Article 8 of the Act.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 49</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the virtual assets or funds in a virtual asset account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the virtual asset service provider subsequently receives a notification for the earmarking of proceeds of fraud in the virtual asset account, the virtual asset service provider shall still be required to earmark the proceeds of fraud in the form of virtual assets or funds, but priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure for such virtual assets or funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 50</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Virtual asset service providers shall, to the extent possible, set up a dedicated 24-hour joint defense notification contact window to carry out the joint defense notification mechanisms.
Virtual asset service providers shall immediately notify the Taiwan Virtual Asset Service Provider Association when they set up the contact window in the preceding paragraph, and the same applies when the contact window is changed.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 51</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the customer of a virtual asset account with seized virtual assets or funds has any doubts regarding the seizure of his or her virtual assets or funds, the customer shall contact the judicial police authority that reported the watch-listed virtual asset account to resolve the matter. The virtual asset service provider shall also provide assistance where necessary.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>   Chapter 5 Return of Remaining Funds or Virtual Assets</編章節>
  <編章節>      Section 1 Deposit Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 52</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If a deposit account suspected of involvement in fraud has been reported as a watch-listed deposit account, and there are still unwithdrawn funds remitted (transferred) by a victim in the account, when the judicial police authority notifies the deposit business institution in writing to return the remaining funds in the watch-listed deposit account to the victim, with a copy of the notification sent to the account holder, the deposit business institution may proceed with the return upon receipt of the written notification.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 53</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a deposit business institution implements measures in accordance with the preceding article, it shall notify the victims through the remitting (transferring) deposit business institutions or electronic payment institutions to prepare the following documents. Thereafter, based on the chronological order of inward remittances (transfers), the deposit business institution shall identify, transaction by transaction, the portions that have not yet been withdrawn or transferred, and return the remaining money held in the watch-listed account to victims, starting from the amount of the last transaction and working backward until the balance of the watch-listed deposit account reaches zero:
1. Identity certification document.
2. A certificate or document of case acceptance (processing) issued by the judicial police authority.
3. An undertaking issued by the victim stating that he or she will bear all liability for any damages incurred by the deposit business institution due to untrue information provided by such victim.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 54</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[With respect to returning the remaining funds held in a watch-listed deposit account pursuant to the preceding two articles, if any of the following occurs, the deposit business institution may settle and close the account, record such remaining money as an account payable, and wait until a person legally having the right to claim such money requests payment:
1.The account balance is below a certain amount, such that the cost of returning would make such return not worthwhile.
2. The institution is unable to contact the victim(s) within three months after receipt of the notification from the judicial police authority.
3. The victim is unwilling to report the case or to claim the money.
After the deposit business institution settles and closes the account in accordance with the preceding paragraph, it shall not lift the effect of the watch-listing on the account holder until it has been notified to lift the watch-listing or the watch-listing period has expired.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 55</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the funds in a deposit account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the deposit business institution subsequently receives a notification from the judicial police authority as described in Article 52 to return the remaining funds in the account, priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure with respect to such funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 2 Electronic Payment Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 56</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If an electronic payment account suspected of involvement in fraud has been reported as a watch-listed electronic payment account, and there are still unwithdrawn funds remitted (transferred) by a victim in the account, when the judicial police authority notifies the electronic payment institution in writing to return the remaining funds in the watch-listed electronic payment account to the victim, with a copy of the notification sent to the account user, the electronic payment institution may proceed with the return upon receipt of the written notification.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 57</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When an electronic payment institution carries out the procedures described in the preceding article, it shall notify the victims through the remitting (transferring) electronic payment institutions or deposit business institutions to prepare the following documents. Thereafter, based on the chronological order of inward remittances (transfers), the electronic payment institution shall identify, transaction by transaction, the portions that have not yet been withdrawn or transferred, and return the remaining money held in the watch-listed account to victims, starting from the amount of the last transaction and working backward until the balance of the watch-listed e-payment account reaches zero:
1. Identity certification document.
2. A certificate or document of case acceptance (processing) issued by the judicial police authority.
3. An undertaking issued by the victim stating that he or she will bear all liability for any damages incurred by the electronic payment institution due to untrue information provided by such victim.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 58</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[With respect to returning the remaining funds held in a watch-listed e-payment account pursuant to the preceding two articles, if any of the following occurs, the electronic payment institution may settle and close the account, record such remaining money as an account payable, and wait until a person legally having the right to claim such money requests payment:
1. The account balance is below a certain amount, such that the cost of returning would make such return not worthwhile.
2. The institution is unable to contact the victim(s) within three months after receipt of the notification from the judicial police authority.
3. The victim is unwilling to report the case or to claim the money.
After the electronic payment institution settles and closes the account in accordance with the preceding paragraph, it shall not lift the effect of the watch-listing on the account user until it has been notified to lift the watch-listing or the watch-listing period has expired.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 59</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the funds in an electronic payment account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the electronic payment institution subsequently receives a notification from the judicial police authority as described in Article 56 to return the remaining funds in the account, priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure with respect to such funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 3 Credit Cards</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 60</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If a credit card settlement number suspected of involvement in fraud has been reported as a watch-listed credit card settlement number, and there are still unwithdrawn funds remitted (transferred) by a victim, when the judicial police authority notifies the credit card business institution in writing to return the remaining funds in the watch-listed credit card settlement number to the victim, with a copy of the notification sent to the cardholder, the credit card business institution may proceed with the return upon receipt of the written notification.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 61</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a credit card business institution implements measures in accordance with the preceding article, if the funds are remitted (transferred) from a deposit business institution or an electronic payment institution, it shall notify the victims through the remitting (transferring) deposit business institutions or electronic payment institutions to prepare the following documents. Thereafter, the credit card business institution shall identify transaction by transaction based on the chronological order of inward remittances (transfers), and return the remaining money held in the watch-listed credit card settlement number to victims:
1. Identity certification document.
2. A certificate or document of case acceptance (processing) issued by the judicial police authority.
3. An undertaking issued by the victim stating that he or she will bear all liability for any damages incurred by the credit card business institution due to untrue information provided by such victim.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 62</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[With respect to returning the remaining funds held in a watch-listed credit card settlement number pursuant to the preceding two articles, if any of the following occurs, the credit card business institution may record such remaining money as an account payable, and wait until a person legally having the right to claim such money requests payment:
1. The account balance is below a certain amount, such that the cost of returning would make such return not worthwhile.
2. The institution is unable to contact the victim(s) within threemonths after receipt of the notification from the judicial police authority.
3. The victim is unwilling to report the case or to claim the money.
After the credit card business institution records the remaining funds in the account as other payables, the credit card business institution shall not lift the effect of the watch-listing on the credit card until it has been notified to lift the watch-listing or the watch-listing period has expired.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 63</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the funds in a credit card settlement number have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the credit card business institution subsequently receives a notification from the judicial police authority as described in Article 60 to return the remaining funds in the account, priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure with respect to such funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 4 Virtual Asset Accounts</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 64</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If a virtual asset account suspected of involvement in fraud has been reported as a watch-listed virtual asset account, and there are still unwithdrawn virtual assets or funds remitted (transferred) by a victim in the account, the virtual asset service provider shall return the remaining virtual assets or funds in the watch-listed virtual asset account to the victim after receiving a written notification from the judicial police authority that provided the notification to the virtual asset service provider, and notify the customer holding the virtual asset account.
When a virtual asset service provider returns the remaining virtual assets in a watch-listed virtual asset account in accordance with the preceding paragraph, it may first sell the remaining virtual assets in the watch-listed virtual asset account through the virtual asset service provider, and then return the proceeds of such sale to the victim.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 65</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[When a virtual asset service provider carries out the procedures described in the preceding article, it shall notify the victims through the remitting (transferring) virtual asset service provider, deposit business institution, or electronic payment institution to prepare the following documents. Thereafter, based on the chronological order of inward remittances (transfers), the virtual asset service provider shall identify, transaction by transaction, the portions that have not yet been withdrawn or transferred, and return the remaining virtual assets or funds held in the watch-listed account to victims, starting from the amount of the last transaction and working backward until the balance of virtual assets or funds in the account reaches zero:
1. Identity certification document.
2. A certificate or document of case acceptance (processing) issued by the judicial police authority.
3. An undertaking issued by the victim stating that he or she will bear all liability for any damages incurred by the virtual asset service provider due to untrue information provided by such victim.
When virtual asset service providers process the return of remaining virtual assets or funds in a watch-listed virtual asset account, other virtual asset service providers, deposit business institutions, and electronic payment institutions shall, within the necessary scope, cooperate to provide information required for the return operations, including remitting account information, remittance time, remitted amount, virtual asset accounts, and other information sufficient to confirm the order and amount of the return.
The fields, format, timing of provision, notification methods, and operating procedures for the information in the preceding paragraph shall be formulated by the Taiwan Virtual Asset Service Provider Association in consultation with the Bankers Association of the Republic of China and the Electronic Payment Association of R.O.C., and reported to the competent authority for record.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 66</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[With respect to returning the remaining virtual assets or funds held in a watch-listed virtual asset account pursuant to the preceding two articles, if any of the following occurs, the virtual asset service provider may settle and close the account, record such remaining virtual assets or funds as a virtual asset payable or an account payable, and wait until a person legally having the right to claim such assets requests payment:
1. The remaining virtual assets or funds are below a certain amount, such that the cost of returning would make such return not worthwhile.
2. The institution is unable to contact the victim(s) within three months after receipt of the notification from the judicial police authority.
3. The victim is unwilling to report the case or to claim the virtual assets or funds.
After the virtual asset service provider settles and closes the account in accordance with the preceding paragraph, it shall not lift the effect of the watch-listing on the account holder until it has been notified to lift the watch-listing or the watch-listing period has expired.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 67</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[If the virtual assets or funds in a virtual asset account have been seized, preserved, prohibited, or subjected to similar measures under another law, and the virtual asset service provider subsequently receives a notification from the judicial police authority described in Article 64 to return the remaining virtual assets or funds in the account, priority shall be given to the order for the seizure, preservation, prohibition, or similar measure with respect to such virtual assets or funds.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>      Section 5 Supervising Officer and Cases Where Assets Cannot be Returned</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 68</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Deposit business institutions, electronic payment institutions, credit card business institutions, and virtual asset service providers shall designate a deputy general manager or officer of equivalent level to supervise the handling of balances or virtual assets held in watch-listed deposit accounts, watch-listed electronic payment accounts, watch-listed credit card settlement numbers, or watch-listed virtual asset accounts.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 69</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Cases identified by deposit business institutions, electronic payment institutions, credit card business institutions, or virtual asset service providers as being suspected of involving transaction disputes or otherwise complicated shall be handled through judicial procedures, and the rules regarding return of remaining funds or virtual assets in these Regulations shall not apply thereto.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>   Chapter 6 Operations of the Fraud Prevention Platform</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 70</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[To establish a fraud prevention platform, the establishing institution shall submit the following documents to the FSC to apply for approval:
1. Operational proposal specifying matters such as the purpose of establishing the fraud prevention platform, participating institutions, operational structure and workflow, risk and benefit assessment, and expected implementation schedule.
2. Explanation of the scope and necessity of customer information collected, processed, and used by participating institutions of the fraud prevention platform.
3. Agreements, templates, or explanations regarding rights and obligations among related parties of the fraud prevention platform.
4. Explanation of the information system and security control operations of the fraud prevention platform.
5. Other documents required by the FSC.
A fraud prevention platform that, prior to the amendment and promulgation of these Regulations on July 20, 2026, was established after being reported to the FSC shall be deemed to have obtained the FSC’s approval.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 71</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[Participating institutions of the fraud prevention platform may use the services provided by the fraud prevention platform to perform the following operations:
1. Analysis or identification of abnormal deposit accounts, electronic payment accounts, credit cards, or virtual asset accounts suspected of involvement in fraud pursuant to these Regulations.
2. Operations related to inquiries, reporting, and account control measures pursuant to these Regulations.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 72</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[To implement anti-fraud measures prescribed by the Act and these Regulations, the establishing institution and participating institutions of the fraud prevention platform may collect, process, and use customer information of participating institutions through the fraud prevention platform within the necessary scope.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
  <編章節>   Chapter 7 Supplementary Provisions</編章節>
  <條文>
    <條號>Article 73</條號>
    <條文內容><![CDATA[These Regulations shall enter into force on the date of promulgation.]]></條文內容>
  </條文>
</法規內容>
</法規>
